# .gitignore — generated by hypo init
# Excludes Hypomnema runtime files that contain machine-specific or session PII.

# Runtime cache: sync-state.json contains hostname() and timestamps
.cache/

# Append-lock files: transient <target>.lock guards around session-log / log.md
# writes (crystallize apply, deriveRootLogEntries). Normally deleted immediately;
# a crashed holder can leave a stale one, which must never be committed.
*.lock
# The lock is published by linking a staged sibling into place. `*.lock` does not
# match the staging name, and a crash between the link and its cleanup leaves one
# behind — where `git add -A` would happily pick it up.
*.lock.*.tmp

# Migration backup of a hand-authored root hot.md, written the first time
# writeRootHotProjection takes over a file it does not already own (see
# hooks/hypo-shared.mjs). Never tracked: it can hold whatever a person's own
# uncommitted notes held, and a scoped auto-commit must never pick it up.
/hot.md.pre-projection-backup*.md
# atomicWrite's own temp file for the backup write above
# (`<backupPath>.<pid>.<random>.tmp`): carries the same hand-authored bytes
# until the rename that produces the file matched above, so a kill or power
# loss mid-write must not leave it exposed to `git add -A` either.
/hot.md.pre-projection-backup*.tmp
